# MediScribe AI — environment variables
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values. `.env` is git-ignored; never commit it.

# ── Required ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# PostgreSQL connection string.
#   Local hybrid dev : scripts/dev-backend.sh overrides this to localhost:5432
#   Docker compose   : use the "db" service hostname
#   Railway          : injected automatically by the Postgres plugin — do not set
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://mediscribe:mediscribe_dev_password@db:5432/mediscribe

# Secret used to sign JWTs. Generate one with:
#   python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
# Rotating this invalidates every existing session token.
JWT_SECRET_KEY=replace-with-a-64-char-hex-secret

# Groq API configuration for SOAP note generation. Keep API key on backend only.
GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_replace_me
GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile

# ── Optional ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Comma-separated list of allowed browser origins (scheme + host, no trailing
# slash). Defaults to a set of localhost dev origins when unset.
# CORS_ORIGINS=https://your-frontend.vercel.app

# Application log level (DEBUG exposes transcript previews — keep at INFO in prod).
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# ASR configuration. Defaults shown; only faster-whisper is supported at deploy.
# WHISPER_BACKEND=faster-whisper
# WHISPER_MODEL=small.en
# WHISPER_COMPUTE_TYPE=int8
# WHISPER_BEAM_SIZE=3

# ── Model providers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Which provider serves the pipeline. Leave at groq unless you intend to
# re-baseline: every committed result in backend/eval/results/ was produced by
# GROQ_MODEL on Groq, and changing the generating model invalidates every
# before/after comparison recorded in context/MODEL_ROADMAP.md.
# LLM_PROVIDER=groq
# GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# The evaluation judge. Pointing it at a different provider does two things:
# it stops evaluation competing with the pipeline for one 200,000 token/day
# quota, and it stops the pipeline grading its own homework, which inflates
# agreement for reasons unrelated to note quality.
#
# Supported providers: groq, gemini, cerebras. Set the matching key below.
# Unset, the judge falls back to the pipeline provider and model — but only
# within one provider. Naming a different provider without also naming a model
# is refused, because a model name does not carry across providers.
#
# Pick a PINNED model, not a `-latest` alias and not a `-preview`. A judge whose
# model changes underneath it makes scores from different runs incomparable,
# which defeats the point of having a judge at all.
#
# Confirm the model name exists before relying on it:
#   cd backend && python -m scripts.check_model_access
# That lists what each provider actually offers. A model name that does not
# exist is how this project once served its fallback note for every request
# without saying so.
#
# Gemini notes, all measured rather than taken from documentation:
#  - Free limits are per model, per day, and specific to your account. They are
#    not published; read them at https://aistudio.google.com/rate-limit.
#    Reach for the Lite tier, not Flash: every full Flash model (3.8, 3.7, 3.6,
#    3.5, 3, 2.5) allows 5 requests/minute and 20/day, while
#    gemini-3.5-flash-lite allows 15/minute and 500/day for no measurable
#    difference in judging quality. Picking "the newest Flash" buys the same 20
#    requests as the oldest.
#  - Appearing in the model list does not mean you can call it: `gemini-2.5-flash`
#    lists fine and then 404s with "no longer available to new users".
#  - Reasoning tokens are charged against `max_tokens`. A 90-item judge prompt
#    spent 2,900 of a 3,000 budget thinking and returned truncated JSON.
#    GROQ_REASONING_EFFORT=low is forwarded to Gemini and fixes this; it halved
#    total tokens with byte-identical output.
# EVAL_JUDGE_PROVIDER=gemini
# EVAL_JUDGE_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# CEREBRAS_API_KEY=
